&lt;p&gt;I came across an interesting plan by a group of webmasters to rate limit the speed of hosted sites for members of the FCC so they could get a taste of what the end of Net Neutrality would mean.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The webmasters are rate limiting all web requests to their hosts if the users are coming from FCC IP addresses. The code to limit has been posted on a gist &lt;a href="https://gist.github.com/kyledrake/e6046644115f185f7af0" title="How to throttle the FCC to dial up modem speeds on your website using Nginx" target="_blank"&gt;here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
